---
import AboutHubNav from "../../components/AboutHubNav.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Zapier & Make integration">
  <article class="card max-w-3xl mx-auto my-8">
    <AboutHubNav currentSlug="zapier-integration" />
    <h1 class="card-title">Zapier & Make.com</h1>
    <p class="card-subtitle">
      Connect ThermalTrace to thousands of apps using inbound webhooks (Pro) and outbound alert webhooks.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Triggers (ThermalTrace → Zapier)</h2>
    <p class="text-sm mb-3">
      Enable <strong>Outbound webhook</strong> under Dashboard → Alerts (Pro). Point Zapier’s
      <strong>Webhooks by Zapier → Catch Hook</strong> at your URL. Each alert POSTs JSON:
    </p>
    <pre class="text-xs overflow-x-auto mb-4"><code>{`{
  "title": "Temperature alert",
  "body": "Garage is 33.2°F …",
  "kind": "threshold",
  "sent_at": "2026-08-28T12:00:00.000Z"
}`}</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Actions (Zapier → ThermalTrace)</h2>
    <p class="text-sm mb-3">
      Create an <strong>Inbound webhook</strong> on Dashboard → Share (Pro). Use
      <strong>Webhooks by Zapier → POST</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm space-y-1 mb-4">
      <li><code>POST /api/inbound/&lt;token&gt;</code> with body <code>action=snooze, hours=24</code></li>
      <li><code>action=vacation, hours=168</code></li>
      <li><code>action=status</code> — returns snooze/vacation state</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Make.com</h2>
    <p class="text-sm mb-3">
      Same URLs — use the HTTP module. Optional HMAC header <code>X-GarageTemp-Signature</code> when a signing secret is configured.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">OpenAPI</h2>
    <p class="text-sm mb-0">
      Full reference: <a class="text-link" href="/docs/api">/docs/api</a> ·
      <a class="text-link" href="/openapi.yaml">openapi.yaml</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
